# core::iter - the standard iteration protocol.
#
# `Iterator` is Vyb's single iteration contract (see the [DECIDED] aspect-based
# design in TODO.md). A type binds it, assigns the associated `type Item` (what
# the iterator yields), and implements `next`, which returns `Some(value)` for
# each element and `None` once the sequence is exhausted. The receiver is taken
# by reference (`self<their<Self>>`) so `next` can advance internal cursor state
# in place on the caller's object.
#
# A bound iterator is consumed by calling `.next()` in a loop:
#
#   import core::iter
#
#   while (true) {
#       match (it.next()) {
#           Some(v) -> { ... use v ... }
#           None   -> { break }
#       }
#   }
#
# `for (item in it)` desugaring over this protocol is a compiler follow-up; until
# it ships, use the explicit `.next()` / `match` loop above.
#
# This module is explicitly imported (`import core::iter`) — it is not part of the
# auto-imported core contracts module (`core::aspects`), so bind authors keep full
# control over when the `Iterator` name is in scope.

share(all)
aspect Iterator {
    type Item
    next(self<their<Self>>)<Option<Self::Item>> -> { }
}
